        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/queens-domain-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>The clue, of course, is right there in the title. Developer Freshly Baked Games' Queen's Domain isn't <em>just</em> a retro-fantasy action RPG played in first-person; it's an explicit homage to King's Field, the long-dormant FromSoftware series that - as the precursor to Demon's Souls, Dark Souls, Bloodborne, Sekiro, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/elden-ring-walkthrough-8042\">Elden Ring</a>, and all those other Soulslikes - helped shape the modern gaming landscape in its own small way. That, though, is pretty much where my knowledge of the series begins and ends - as much as I love FromSoftware, I've never actually played a King's Field game. I've no idea how Queen's Domain shapes up as Kings Field-like, then, but I do know that, five or so hours in, it's already one of my favourite games this year.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/queens-domain-now-playing\">Rea",
